    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0613" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13533: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-12T12:00:00+08:00">June 12,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 12—6:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Substance of Nanking’s June 11, 9 a.m.,<anchor n="75" xml:id="d541-f1"/> and June
                    11, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="76" xml:id="d541-f2"/> is being communicated to Navy to
                    be forwarded to Admiral Allen. U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi>
                    will leave Hankow for Changsha morning of June 13th.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Department, Peiping and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
